required.hint:
Pricing model. Accepts shorthand strings OR a full object.

Shorthand: "ondemand", "spot", or committed shorthands like "instanceSavings3yrAllUpfront", "computeSavings1yrNoUpfront".

Full object (recommended for committed pricing):
- EC2 Instance Savings Plans: {"model":"instanceSavings","term":"1 Year","upfrontPayment":"None"}
- Compute Savings Plans: {"model":"computeSavings","term":"1 Year","upfrontPayment":"None"}
- Standard Reserved Instances (dedicated/host tenancy only): {"model":"reserved","term":"1 Year","upfrontPayment":"None"} (alias "standard" also accepted)
- Convertible Reserved Instances (dedicated/host tenancy only): {"model":"convertible","term":"1 Year","upfrontPayment":"None"}

Valid term values: "1 Year", "3 Year" (shorthands "1yr"/"3yr" also accepted)
Valid upfrontPayment values: "None", "Partial", "All" (case-insensitive; "No Upfront" style accepted)

Display labels like "EC2 Instance Savings Plans" are also accepted and normalized. Any value that does not resolve is REJECTED at add_service with the valid values listed — nothing silently falls back to On-Demand. EstimateBuilder normalizes via lib/ec2.js.
